+# 0.29.0
+
+- Added fail-closed `losica-causal-stream/1` projection.
+- Made continuous numeric experience the default generation input.
+- Learned multi-step events and lexical regions from held-out future-sample reconstruction.
+- Learned semantic partitions and ordered constructions from recurring message use.
+- Added exact generation and membership replay.
+- Moved Concepticon, CLICS, WALS, English, and other human analyses to the legacy or adapter path.
+- Added separate post-generation external alignment records.
+- Generated productive bound markers from recurring region-host distributions.
+- Added compositional realization and utterance-to-region analysis.
+- Added usage-driven fusion, boundary loss, and stored-root lexical reanalysis.
+- Preserved source decomposition as historical provenance after current analysis becomes one root.
+- Added bidirectional use of separate human-language alignment files.
+- Removed adapter records that manually assign generated region identities.
+- Added source-time alignment from descriptions to recorded experience.
+- Added cross-situation phrase learning and an explicit 80% translation coverage gate.
